<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">brew</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">brew</ansi> refills every Alchemist's flask satchel in your company from the
reagents in your pack: one reagent makes one flask, the first Alchemist first
(you, then your companions by number). It works anywhere out of battle and
never advances the world clock.

  <ansi fg="command">brew</ansi>

It says how many flasks each Alchemist brewed and how many reagents are left
(<ansi fg="command">Reagents carried: N.</ansi>). A full satchel takes no reagents. With no reagents it
says so; with no Alchemist in your company it says no one throws flasks.

A camp rest does the same on its own when it ends (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>). Reagents are sold in
Dunmar's market and never bought back; each new Alchemist starts with a few.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help alchemist</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>.
